// Payout schedule determines when funds are released to payees.
// Dates are computed by `computePayoutDate`
// (packages/core/src/lib/payout-scheduling), at midnight America/Chicago.
//
// CORRECTED 2026-09: the previous comment here claimed "all schedules respect
// a 2-day post-event floor for refund handling". No such floor was ever
// implemented, and ASAP is event end + 1 day, not 2. What DOES clamp maturity
// is the Stripe balance-availability floor applied when the ledger credit is
// written (`applyAvailabilityFloor`): a flat 2 business days from the charge,
// every payment method. That is a funds-availability guard, not a refund
// window. See `settlement-availability.ts` for why there is no ACH branch.
enum PayoutSchedule {
  ASAP               // The day after the event ends (fastest possible)
  WEEK_OF_EVENT      // Sunday of the event's week, rolled to the FOLLOWING Sunday when that Sunday is < 2 days after the event (Sat/Sun events)
  ONE_WEEK_AFTER     // Sunday of the following week
  TWO_WEEKS_AFTER    // Sunday 2 weeks after event week (DEFAULT for new payout terms)
  FOUR_WEEKS_AFTER   // Sunday 4 weeks after event week (~1 month)
}

